  "finalText": "**Task completed.**\n\nI've processed the cancellation of reservation R3311 for Marcus Bell. Here's what happened:\n\n**Settlement:** $248.00 issued as **travel credit** (not back to his card)\n\n**Why not a cash refund:**\n- Basic economy fares are non-refundable\n- His trip insurance does override this, BUT only pays cash back to the card if cancellation is made **at least 14 days before departure**\n- He's canceling on 2026-07-28 for a flight on 2026-08-05—just 8 days away\n- When canceling within 14 days, the insurance policy converts the fare into travel credit instead of returning cash to his card\n\n**Actions taken:**\n1. ✓ Issued $248.00 as travel credit to his account\n2. ✓ Cancelled reservation R3311 and released his seat\n\nMarcus will need to use the $248 travel credit for a future flight rather than receiving cash on his card, as required by the insurance terms for cancellations made close to departure.",
